1703 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Mark Cerny is a veteran game designer and architect whose credits include hits like Crash Bandicoot\054 Jak \046 Daxter\054 and Uncharted\056 At D\056I\056C\056E\056 2002 he distilled decades of studio experience into METHOD\054 a philosophy built around ruthless early prototyping\054 a concise \034macro\035 design\054 and data\055driven play\055testing\073 ensuring projects prove their fun before sinking into full production\056 \n\nA development philosophy distilled into four non\055linear keystones for de\055risking and driving creative game projects\072\n\nPre\055Production vs Production\nPublishable First Playable\nMacro \0505\055page\051 vs Micro Design\nRigorous Gameplay Testing\n\nWhat Works for UIW3D Studio\nClear Prototype Goal\n\034Publishable\035 slice mirrors our Workshop prototype and Stubbing milestones\054 giving students a tangible win\056\nLight Macro Design\nConcise bibles synched with our 16\055week course keeps docs manageable\056\nPlay\055Testing Ethos\nObservational feedback sessions map directly to our strike\055team reviews and QA Complete phase\056\n\nWhat Doesn\031t Fit UIW3D Studio\nChaotic Pre\055Production\nCerny\031s \034manage chaos\035 clashes with our structured\054 credit\055bearing 16\055week course\nOur students need clearly sequenced checkpoints\056\nMinimal Documentation\nA 5\055page macro doc leaves too much ambiguity for interdisciplinary student teams\073 we could benefit from richer documentation and asset catalogs\056\nBinary Kill Criterion\nCanceling on a single prototype isn\031t the play\054 especially in education\n\n)
     /K [ 19 ]
     /P 1704 0 R
     /Pg 1665 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

