3291 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Art\057Game Development Solution \055 We separate engine specific files\054 from the individual assets that make up the final in\055game asset\056\n\nSource Art \055 All the assets\054 scene files\054 resources\054 etc\056 I used to create the final in\055game content\056 \n \nProduction Art \055 Final in\055engine content\056 \n\nDeveloper Content Creation Tools \050DCC\051 \055 Software like\072 ZBrush\054 Maya\054 Blender\054 Substance Painter\054 Designer\054 Marvelous Designer\056\056\056\056\n\nQuality of life \055 Takes away confusion\056 We can upload specific version of the engine\054 for everyone to use\041  \n\nAvoids clutter in the engine\n\nAllows for a more nuanced iterative and collaborative production process\056\n\n\nI can work in cohesion with another artist\054 share files\054 push updates\054 get latest all in a very structured file directory that states where the Source Art is that made the final assets that ended up in\055engine\056\n\nRelieves Bottlenecks \055 If I get sick\054 for 10 days\056 It doesn\031t matter to the studio in regards to my assets and tasks\056 They can reallocate the work to another artist\054 and pick up where I left off\056 If I leave the studio\054 an artist who may need to fix bugs or upres my asset or create lods\054 have all the source assets they need to do\056 \n\n\n)
     /K [ 813 ]
     /P 3292 0 R
     /Pg 1665 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

