  << /ActualText (FADE IN\072\nINT\056 SCHOOL HALLWAY \055 EARLY MORNING\n\nA quiet\054 sunlit hallway\056 Fluorescent lights hum faintly\056 The world is still\056\n\nMILES \05012\051\054 backpack neatly in place\054 walks into frame \055 calm\054 focused\056 He stops at LOCKER 214\056\n\nHe exhales\056 Spins the lock\072 left\054 right\054 left\056 Click\056\n\nThe locker door swings open\054 revealing a meticulously arranged interior\072\nColor\055coded folders\nStacked notebooks\nPencil box aligned to a tape grid\nLaminated checklist taped inside\n\nMiles begins his morning ritual\056\n\nHe adjust a folder\031s angle\056 Checks a pencil\056 Runs his fingers down the checklist\056 \nSatisfied\056 \n\nHe pulls the locker door closed\056 It resists\056 \nHe tugs again\056 A beat \055 \n\nSNAP\041\n\nThe door burst open \055 \n\nFLASHCARDS scatter\056 A sandwich tumbles\056 A socks rolls out\056\n\nMiles freezes\056\nA beat\056 His breath quickens\056 \n\nHe drops to his knees\054 scrambling\072 \nSorting flashcards by color\nFlattening crumpled papers\nRe\055stacking folders\054 trembling\n\nNothing fits\056 One flashcard is bent\056 \n\nThe system is broken\056 )
