  << /ActualText (MacOS Development \055 Git Setup\n\n\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\n\nGit is a version control system\054 meaning it tracks changes to files over time\056 This lets you work safely\054 go back in time\054 or collaborate with others\056 \n\nVerify Git\n \174 git \055\055version\n\n\n\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\n\nGit tracks who made changes\056 These settings tell Git your identity so commits are labeled with your name\057email \050must match GitHub to associate commits to your profile\051\056\n\nConfigure Git Identity\n\174 git config \055\055global user\056name \034ProfessorGarcia\035\n\174 git config \055\055global user\056email \034cagarc12\100uiwtx\056edu\035\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\n\nSSH Keys are like digital ID cards\056 Instead of typing your GitHub password every time\054 your computer proves your identity using a private\057public key pair\056 You keep the private key on your Mac\073 GitHub stores the public key\056\n\nGenerate SSH Key\n\174 ssh\055keygen \055t ed25519 \055C \034cagarc12\100uiwtx\056edu\035\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\n\nThe public key is handing someone your ID\055they can verify you\054 but they can\031t impersonate you\056 GitHub saves it so your Mac can push\057pull to repos securely without a password\056 \n\nCopy Public Key to GitHub\n\174 cat \176\057\056ssh\057id\137ed25519\056pub\n\n\n\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\n\nThis command confirms the trust relationship is working\056 It\031s like saying\072 \034Hey GitHub\054 its me\035 and GitHub replies\054 \034Welcome back\054 trusted device\056\035\n\nTest SSH Connection\n\174 ssh \055T git\100github\056com\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\n\nCross\055Device Development is now Setup\nClone any repo \050including game\055learning repos\051\nPush\057Pull code from my Mac just like my PC\nAvoid re\055entering passwords thanks to SSH\n\n\n\n\n\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055\055)
     /K [ 0 ]
